# Build-context hygiene for `docker build` (COPY . . in the Dockerfile).
# gitignore does NOT limit what is sent to the builder: a dirty working tree
# would otherwise ship local secrets, data and caches into build layers and
# the cache. Keep this list aligned with .gitignore and with what the build
# truly needs (see infra/tests/test_dockerignore.py).

# VCS metadata
.git

# Dependencies (installed fresh via npm ci in the image)
**/node_modules

# Build outputs (rebuilt inside the image)
**/dist
**/build

# Local env files and secrets. The committed examples stay: they are part of
# the source tree and carry no secrets.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local runtime state and creator/investor secrets (never part of a build)
backend/.creator.json
backend/.demo-investors.json
backend/data
backend/debug-ops.ts
data/community-store.json
deploy

# Logs, OS noise, caches, test/coverage artifacts
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/coverage
frontend/test-results
frontend/playwright-report
frontend/screenshots
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Rust build/test output (the image never builds contracts)
contracts/crowdfund/target
contracts/crowdfund/contracts/crowdfund/test_snapshots

# Local-only unverified skill copies and portal build trees
docs/skills-reference/private
portal/build-public
portal/build-internal
portal/.docusaurus
